{"challenge_axes":[],"difficulty":3,"generation_seed":20261009,"generator_version":"1.1.0","oracle_version":"independent-1.0.0","producer_agent_id":"/root","producer_role":"improvement_engineer","record_hash":"6f3fe58f8e838386060fdd5f2a998e620df40b81fd0a771c2a30e269a37dcecc","rendered_input":"Executable task contract:\nJSON scalar values in this task are null, boolean, integer (excluding boolean), or string. No floating point or coercion is used. Scalar equality is type-sensitive. Malformed tasks are outside the valid-task domain.\nInput: `modules` is a list of `{module_id:string,capabilities:[distinct_strings],priority:integer}` with distinct module IDs. `memory` maps strings to JSON scalar values (null, boolean, integer excluding boolean, or string). `protected` lists distinct keys already in memory. `requests` is an ordered list of `{request_id:string,needs:[distinct_strings],writes:[{key:string,value:JSON_scalar}]}` with distinct request IDs. A module is eligible exactly when its capabilities contain every need; an empty needs list admits every module. Choose the eligible module with smallest (priority,module_id), using ordinary string lexicographic order for the second component. If none is eligible, selected_module is null (abstention), no writes are attempted, and blocked_writes is empty. Otherwise execute the request's writes in order. Ignore each write whose key is protected and report its zero-based index in blocked_writes; all other writes replace or create that memory entry. Protection applies throughout the task, so protected values retain their initial values. Return exactly `{routes:[{request_id,selected_module:string_or_null,eligible_modules:[module_ids_sorted_lexicographically],blocked_writes:[integer_indices]}],memory:final_memory_map}` with routes in request order. Competence is explicitly declared in capabilities; this task does not infer or train module competence.\nTask JSON:\n{\"requests\":[{\"writes\":[{\"value\":\"overwrite\",\"key\":\"seal\